# Already-compressed evidence: do not try to compress or delta it.
#
# ~15,500 tracked files in this repo are gzip/JPEG/PNG/PDF streams. Git's default
# zlib pass and delta search cannot shrink them — measured on 3,000 of the
# geo_sweep .json.gz traces, the default pack was 146,283,926 bytes and a pack
# with compression and delta disabled was 146,284,199 bytes. That is a 273-byte
# "saving" across 146 MB (0.0002%) bought with double the packing CPU. On a
# single .gz blob, git's zlib pass makes the object 0.04% LARGER than the input.
#
# `binary` = -diff -merge -text: never line-diff or eol-convert these, which also
# stops a stray text conversion from corrupting a byte of evidence.
# `-delta` skips the delta search that cannot pay off on compressed streams.

*.gz    binary -delta
*.jpg   binary -delta
*.jpeg  binary -delta
*.png   binary -delta
*.webp  binary -delta
*.mp4   binary -delta
*.webm  binary -delta
*.pdf   binary -delta
*.zip   binary -delta
